{
  "$schema": "https://appflare.github.io/catalog/schema/v1.json",
  "slug": "gentlemail",
  "name": "GentleMail",
  "summary": "Multi-domain webmail, email API and webhooks on Workers, D1, R2, Email Routing and Email Service.",
  "tagline": "Webmail for all your domains, with an email API and webhooks",
  "features": [
    "Receive and send mail for any number of domains and mailboxes from one install",
    "Choose which people can open which mailboxes, with two-step sign-in",
    "Read mail in conversations, with search, attachments and a spam folder",
    "Send and read mail from your own code with scoped API keys",
    "Get signed webhooks the moment mail arrives or is sent",
    "Let AI assistants such as Claude search and answer mail, asking before they send"
  ],
  "repo": "Softwaiz/gentlemail",
  "homepage": "https://gentlemail.dev",
  "license": "MIT",
  "categories": ["email", "business"],
  "authors": [{ "name": "Softwaiz", "url": "https://gentlemail.dev", "github": "Softwaiz" }],
  "maintainers": ["MendyLanda"],
  "source": { "ref": "v0.8.1", "sha": "efe93cd3a85b0b653a89da28c448412e04786a62" },
  "install": {
    "packageManager": "pnpm",
    // The source config. The Worker is built with RedwoodSDK and Cloudflare's
    // Vite plugin, which writes the bundled Worker and its deploy config under
    // apps/mail/dist and points wrangler at it through
    // apps/mail/.wrangler/deploy/config.json; the packer follows that redirect.
    "wranglerConfig": "apps/mail/wrangler.jsonc",
    // apps/mail/package.json's build script (vite build). It runs in apps/mail,
    // where vite.config.mts reads wrangler.jsonc. The config has no build.command.
    "buildCommand": "pnpm --dir apps/mail run build",
    // Upstream's setup (apps/mail/README.md, "Connect a domain") points the
    // zone's catch-all at the Worker; the email handler rejects mail to an
    // address without a mailbox with a 550 (src/lib/inbound.ts).
    "emailRouting": { "catchAll": true }
  },
  // Upstream requires Workers Paid (README, "What you need"): sending goes
  // through Email Sending, and every sign-in derives a PBKDF2 hash with 100,000
  // iterations, more CPU than the free plan's 10 ms.
  "plan": "paid",
  "requires": ["zone", "email-routing", "r2", "email-placeholders"],
  // Left out: SETUP_TOKEN. Upstream's /setup page takes it once to create the
  // first admin (src/app/pages/auth.tsx). The seed below creates that admin at
  // install instead, and /setup redirects to /login once any user exists.
  "secrets": [
    {
      "name": "ADMIN_PASSWORD",
      "label": "Admin password",
      "help": "The password of the first admin account, at least 10 characters. You can change it later under Admin, Users.",
      "generate": "password",
      "seedOnly": true
    }
  ],
  "vars": [
    {
      "name": "ADMIN_EMAIL",
      "label": "Admin email",
      "help": "You sign in to GentleMail with this address. It does not need a mailbox in GentleMail.",
      "seedOnly": true
    },
    {
      // src/lib/webhooks.ts publicUrl: links in webhook payloads.
      "name": "PUBLIC_URL",
      "label": "Public address",
      "help": "The address GentleMail is served at, used for links in webhook payloads. Appflare fills it in and keeps it in step with a custom domain.",
      "default": "{{appUrl}}"
    },
    {
      // The form starts with the wrangler config's value, GentleMail.
      "name": "APP_NAME",
      "label": "Name",
      "help": "The name shown in the interface and the browser tab."
    },
    {
      "name": "SPAM_SCORE_THRESHOLD",
      "label": "Spam score threshold",
      "help": "Move mail to Spam when Cloudflare's spam score (up to 5, higher is spammier) reaches this number. Leave empty to turn it off; if you turn it on, start at 5.",
      "optional": true
    }
  ],
  "resources": {
    "d1": {
      "DB": {
        // src/lib/auth.ts: hashPassword stores pbkdf2$<iterations>$<salt>$<hash>,
        // PBKDF2-SHA-256 with 100,000 iterations, a 16-byte salt and a 32-byte
        // key, both in padded base64 (btoa); verifyPassword reads the
        // iterations from the stored value. createUser lowercases the email
        // and stores created_at in milliseconds. Ids are only compared, so a
        // random hex id serves as well as upstream's crypto.randomUUID().
        "seed": {
          "hashes": {
            "admin": {
              "from": "ADMIN_PASSWORD",
              "method": "pbkdf2-sha256",
              "iterations": 100000,
              "saltBytes": 16,
              "keyBytes": 32,
              "encoding": "base64"
            }
          },
          "statements": [
            {
              "sql": "INSERT OR IGNORE INTO users (id, email, name, password_hash, role, created_at) VALUES (lower(hex(randomblob(16))), lower(trim(?)), ?, ? || ? || ? || ?, ?, CAST((julianday('now') - 2440587.5) * 86400000 AS INTEGER))",
              "params": [
                { "var": "ADMIN_EMAIL" },
                { "value": "Admin" },
                { "value": "pbkdf2$100000$" },
                { "salt": "admin" },
                { "value": "$" },
                { "hash": "admin" },
                { "value": "admin" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "postInstall": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "Open {{appUrl}} and sign in with the admin email and password you chose. In **Admin → Domains**, add `{{emailDomain}}`, then create mailboxes and users in **Admin**. Appflare already turned on Email Routing for `{{emailDomain}}` and sent its catch-all to GentleMail, so mail to any mailbox you create there arrives; mail to an address without a mailbox is rejected."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "To send from `{{emailDomain}}`, onboard it to Email Sending in the Cloudflare dashboard (**Email Service → Email Sending**), or run `npx wrangler email sending enable {{emailDomain}}`."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "For another domain, run the commands its page in GentleMail shows, but point the catch-all at the Worker **{{workerName}}**: the page names the Worker from the upstream build (`my-gentlemail`)."
    }
  ]
}
